          "document_name": "github__dsid_ae068ee4aa9640159427cd941bef0238.md",
          "version_no": 1,
          "page_from": 1,
          "page_to": 1,
          "anchor": "p-2",
          "heading": "Pr 18421 Multipart File Validation Limits",
          "content": "Ravi Singh: please ensure the validator surfaces clear errors for multipart boundary parsing failures; I saw a flaky crash in an initial run.\nAisha Patel: replied — parser now catches malformed boundary exceptions and returns a 400 with error.type=malformed_multipart and includes low-signal debug id for tracing; updated tests.\nSofia Alvarez: approved — addressed my comments about metrics naming and added a suggestion to include counter tags for tenant_id and route_id.\nCI Bot: integration-tests failed on first run due to test harness timeout; rerun completed successfully.\nQA: noted an edge case where client SDK retries might double-submit large files; added a recommendation in docs and an optional idempotency header support in adapter.\nAdded multipart/form-data support on OpenAI-compat API paths with strict content-type validation and configurable per-file and per-request size limits. Default limits: 10MiB per file, 50MiB per request. Feature is behind a feature flag and can be enabled per-tenant. See docs/openai-compat/multipart.md for migration steps.",
